[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638085312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113854#issuecomment-3638085312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113854","id":3638085312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y2MbA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T17:03:37Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T19:04:10Z","body":"I'd argue the same conditions apply as for `draw_string`, it having multiple lines doesn't necessarily mean it's expected to align the lines based on the maximum width of any one of the lines","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638085312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638434232","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113854#issuecomment-3638434232","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113854","id":3638434232,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y3hm4","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T18:33:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T18:33:09Z","body":"For multiline text, it probably makes sense to use max width.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638434232/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638487586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113854#issuecomment-3638487586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113854","id":3638487586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y3uoi","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T18:47:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T18:47:24Z","body":"You'd expect that with a negative width, Godot would try to fit the text into a region equal to the maximum line width:\n\n<img width=\"164\" height=\"195\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95c5b6d4-cf40-4fcc-99b0-16b0223fbbfa\" />\n\nHowever, Godot interprets a negative width as infinite/unlimited. In this sense, it's simply impossible to align the text; any value other than `HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_LEFT` would result in the text being invisible.\n\n<img width=\"189\" height=\"197\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/654e5aa1-dcb3-4c88-970f-3f152e9a0352\" />\n\nIs it possible to change this behavior? Theoretically, yes, but keep in mind the autowrap modes, which require knowing the width of the region you want to fit the text into. A negative value indicates that this width is unlimited, not that it should be automatically calculated based on the width of the longest line/word in the text.\n\nIn my opinion, we should just add a note or make the existing documentation clearer. I.e. the alignment is ignored with a negative width.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638487586/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638949672","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113854#issuecomment-3638949672","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113854","id":3638949672,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y5fco","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T21:02:34Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:02:34Z","body":"> Godot interprets a negative width as infinite/unlimited. In this sense, it's simply impossible to align the text\n\nWhat's the point of width of -1 then? Godot allows it for some reason. But if it breaks alignment then it's not very useful.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638949672/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638980948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113854#issuecomment-3638980948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113854","id":3638980948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y5nFU","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T21:12:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:12:14Z","body":"> but keep in mind the autowrap modes, which require knowing the width of the region you want to fit the text into.\n\nI do not see any issues with autowrapping, `-1` + autowrap should just wrap only in mandatory break points (`\\n` and similar) which it already does. So `-1` still can be interpreted as \"actual width of text\" / \"automatic\", not infinite.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638980948/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]